---
description: Shared design-token, theme, typography, accessibility, and UI consistency rules.
globs: ["apps/**/*.{css,scss,html,ts,tsx}", "packages/design-system/**/*"]
alwaysApply: false
---

Read @docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md before changing extension-owned UI.

- Use `packages/design-system` as the default visual foundation.
- Pretendard Variable is the default typeface and must be bundled locally through the approved npm dependency; do not load fonts from a CDN at runtime.
- Every UI must work in light, dark, and system theme modes.
- Product code consumes semantic (`--ce-sys-*`) or component (`--ce-comp-*`) tokens. Primitive (`--ce-ref-*`) tokens are for design-system definitions only.
- Do not hard-code colors, shadows, radii, spacing, typography, focus styles, or motion when a suitable token exists.
- If a needed reusable value is missing, add a role-based token to the design system before using it in an app.
- Preserve keyboard focus visibility and accessible contrast.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Injected third-party-page UI must be style-isolated, preferably with Shadow DOM. Do not apply shared global reset/base styles to the host page.
